From 56ef913afe9556525670715b89d59c224eed4846 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:13:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Wind options: blending with the ERA5 10 m wind,
 MicroMet terrain factors

toposcale.wind_downscaling, alone or together:
- surface_blend: u = u_pl + w (u10 - u_pl), w a constant in [0, 1] or the
  terrain weight of the surface-effect correction (clipped to [0, 1]).
  get_era5() fetches the 10 m wind with the surface fields (CDS, GDEX).
- terrain: liston_elder: the wind weighting and diverting factors of
  MicroMet (Liston and Elder 2006) from the slope in the wind direction and
  the terrain curvature (new module wind.py), scaled over the DEM; the
  curvature of a cluster is the mean over its cells.

The pressure-level wind stays the default. The output store records the
options.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
